# lint-staged and tsc must run with cwd=app/: tinyexec (used by lint-staged
# to spawn eslint) resolves node_modules/.bin relative to the real process
# cwd, not the --cwd option, so `cd` first rather than passing `--cwd app`.
cd app

# Full lint is advisory until the pre-existing backlog (~170 errors,
# react-hooks/* and no-explicit-any) is burned down. lint-staged runs eslint on
# staged files and surfaces problems, but does not block the commit, because
# editing any of the ~94 backlog files would otherwise be blocked. Drop the
# `|| echo` to make lint a hard gate once the backlog is cleared (tracked in
# #217).
npx lint-staged || echo "lint reported issues (advisory; see #217 backlog)"

# jsx-a11y IS a hard gate (refs #217 finding 7): all 35 pre-existing
# violations were fixed on this branch, so the ruleset is green today and a
# regression should block the commit. eslint.a11y.config.js enables only
# jsx-a11y rules, so it isn't affected by the advisory backlog above. Runs
# against the whole tree (not just staged files) since it's fast enough.
npx eslint -c eslint.a11y.config.js .

# The two React Compiler correctness rules are also a hard gate (refs #281).
# purity and immutability were brought to zero, and unlike the rest of the
# react-hooks backlog they describe behaviour changes rather than performance
# advice. eslint.correctness.config.js enables only those two.
npx eslint -c eslint.correctness.config.js .

# tsc -b and the commit-msg native-version guard stay hard gates.
npx tsc -b
